L209: These equations show that Na atoms lose electrons while Cl atoms (in the Cl_{2} molecule) gain electrons, the “s” subscripts for the resulting ions signifying they are present in the form of a solid ionic compound. For redox reactions of this sort, the loss and gain of electrons define the complementary processes that occur:
L210: 
